    "executive_summary": "A total of 416 active disaster incidents have been recorded from USGS and NOAA sources. The majority of reported events consist of earthquakes, primarily categorized as low to moderate urgency, alongside various weather-related advisories and warnings including heat, air quality, flood, and small craft conditions. Three high-severity seismic events were documented internationally, including magnitudes between 5.0 and 5.4 in Japan, Peru, and the Philippines, while the remaining incidents span diverse regional impacts. Given the broad geographic distribution and mixed severity levels across seismic and meteorological categories, continued monitoring of ongoing warnings and seismic activity is recommended.",
    "recommendations": [
        "Continue monitoring USGS seismic feeds for aftershocks near recent high-severity earthquake epicenters in Japan, Peru, and the Philippines.",
        "Track active NOAA weather advisories, particularly extreme heat and flood warnings, to ensure timely public safety alerts.",
        "Maintain situational awareness across regional monitoring centers for any escalation in incident urgency levels."
    ]
